// `TODO("why")` is an implementation that has not been written, and it is a compile ERROR
// where it sits. A hole cannot be shipped: the message says what is missing, the span says
// where, and nothing has to be remembered or grepped for.
//
// Its type is `never`, which is the half that makes it usable. A hole stands wherever a
// value is wanted -- a whole function body, one arm of a match, an argument -- and `never`
// is below every type, so the surrounding code still type-checks and the TODO is the ONLY
// error reported. Typing it `()` would bury the message under a second complaint about the
// type the hole should have produced, which is how a marker like this becomes noise.
//
// Both holes below are reported, not just the first: they are ordinary type errors and the
// checker collects them.

